#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571519} :activity/id #uuid "6e4c5edf-99ca-525c-a6e8-fa582f571ea0" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050269 :topic/id #uuid "3b1ff160-959d-503b-acf5-2be698a50baa" :topic/math-academy-id 3595} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571469 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554645 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d738011-9f4c-5d4e-a309-ef64a768c823" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$1\\,200$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554051} {:answer/id #uuid "a9b7e43c-40c5-5e6a-932e-71b4efd2aa35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$1\\,000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554247} {:answer/id #uuid "d48ea0cd-c010-5dea-b3a7-cfb311eab498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$2\\,000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554330} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b52400-e104-580d-9769-33accdba452b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$1\\,500$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554362} {:answer/id #uuid "eb398d66-b3c7-5535-b999-ccfa4a862a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$2\\,500$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554382}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554330} :answer-field/id #uuid "2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fd84baa2-dbd3-5523-aca7-04ab311e0400" :question/math-academy-id "q-134797" :question/problem "![](images/81/815ba0a13bc8cbd7adcfadc63b80d6f2da36c9755166694915fa2f297be27721.png)\n\nAn employee of a car dealership collects data on the value $y$ (in thousands of dollars) of a particular car model $x$ years after its release to the market. The scatter plot for the data and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(6,12).$ So, our actual value is $y=12.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=6$ has the $y$-coordinate $10.$ So, our estimated value is $\\overset{^}{y}=10.$\n\n![](images/ab/ab5e194ac03482b1cee6bdb7aa35e323b40a1ad63769e60acbb000adb7aa1e82.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =12-10 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $$2\\,000.$"} :step/id #uuid "2c0eb85e-9eec-5f4f-b6fc-97a5c56860cb"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571487 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176344 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "876ae649-11c0-5089-87dc-610f0036aa66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174323} {:answer/id #uuid "bc491ea0-1e09-56eb-9a79-d9be42023692" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174324} {:answer/id #uuid "2cf618da-5927-578f-8feb-6bd70f6b8776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174325} {:answer/id #uuid "628ea2d3-dc5f-50b2-81c5-9a43908bb256" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174326} {:answer/id #uuid "6dda488a-d9e3-59a8-81f5-6f9dde1a3f57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174327}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6d0d5456-fec0-5301-ba47-002165462cdb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7ae43775-06ac-519f-ac5d-57c73d122d92" :question/math-academy-id "q-134285" :question/problem "![](images/0e/0e3debd878c7c147ce9978bec054fc9d5c9a490bd094060ec1dd3c6ad56ecac9.png)\n\nAn antique broker has records about the value of an artwork $y$ (in thousands of dollars) at certain times $t$ (in decades) since the artwork was produced. The residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on this data set. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. When $t = 5$, the regression equation underestimates the value of $y$.\n2. The residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n3. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data."} :step/id #uuid "749adcf2-3609-57ef-a88a-58f98584fb0f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571469}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571519 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176342 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a774593d-dc82-5d50-8667-fb9ab35ab5db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$(-10000)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174311} {:answer/id #uuid "be631636-35f9-5288-8344-819217c75758" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$5000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174312} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a353ec-507e-5e8c-a1d6-f5c33eae2784" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$(-5000)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174313} {:answer/id #uuid "fac8b2f2-21e2-5ba4-9832-76e2f12eff72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$10000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174314} {:answer/id #uuid "7a22e90f-667d-50ab-9770-629412ff6774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174315}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6dc00c1c-9fd6-5d82-925a-2adc1e918fcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218604549